# ==============================================================================
# IO72: TREP WebSocket Mid-Price Contribution (Java)
# Java Generation & Evaluation: (not yet run -- update after first unsandboxed run)
# Explanation: (fill in from test-report.md)
# ==============================================================================
# Author: Mike Nimer <mikenimer@google.com>
#
# Pipeline Specification: IO72 - TrepWsIO Source -> ParDo -> TrepWsIO Sink (WebSocket API Post bridge)
# DAG: TrepWsIO.read() (ERT token auth + service discovery; password from Secret Manager)
#      -> Compute Mid Price (ParDo)
#      -> TrepWsIO Sink bridge: DoFn posting Update messages to an internal ADS contribution service
#         via the documented Refinitiv WebSocket API (tr_json2 Login + off-stream Post with Ack).
# Credentials: passwordSecret is a Secret Manager SHORT ID, never the password.
nodes:
  - id: "source-trepws-1"
    type: pipeline
    position:
      x: 80
      y: 150
    data:
      label: "Read TREP FX Quotes"
      type: SOURCE
      iconName: Radio
      beam_transform: TrepWsIO
      properties:
        username: "GE-A-01103867-3-1234"
        ertAuthEnabled: true
        passwordSecret: "trep-ert-password"
        ertAuthStoreLocation: "gs://acme-dataflow-temp/trep-token-store"
        serviceDiscovery: true
        region: "eu"
        instrumentTuples:
          - service: "ELEKTRON_DD"
            rics: "EUR=, JPY=, GBP="
            fields: "BID, ASK"
        cachedFields: "PROD_PERM"
        maxMounts: 1
        timeout: 60000
      system_instructions: >-
        Use the community Refinitiv TrepWsIO connector: Maven com.refinitiv.beamio:trepws-io:1.2.0 (this artifact is NOT
        on Maven Central; add an XML comment in pom.xml and a README Prerequisites step saying it must first be installed
        into the local Maven repository with "mvn install -DskipTests" from https://github.com/Refinitiv/trep-websockets-beam-io).
        In pom.xml add an exclusion of com.google.cloud.dataflow:google-cloud-dataflow-java-sdk-all on that dependency so the
        baseline beam.version is the only Beam on the classpath.
        Imports: com.refinitiv.beamio.trepwebsockets.TrepWsIO, com.refinitiv.beamio.trepwebsockets.TrepWsIO.InstrumentTuple,
        com.refinitiv.beamio.trepwebsockets.MarketPriceMessage. TrepWsIO.read() returns PCollection<MarketPriceMessage> and is an
        UNBOUNDED streaming source: call options.setStreaming(true) and pass --streaming=true in the runner scripts.
        Property mapping: username -> .withUsername(username); ertAuthEnabled true -> .withTokenAuth(true);
        passwordSecret is a Google Cloud Secret Manager secret ID -> resolve it once in main with the accessSecret helper
        (projectId from options.getProject()) and pass it to .withPassword(...); ertAuthStoreLocation -> .withTokenStore(...);
        serviceDiscovery true -> .withServiceDiscovery(true) (no hostname is needed); region -> .withRegion(region);
        instrumentTuples -> .withInstrumentTuples(java.util.List.of(InstrumentTuple.of(service, list of trimmed RICs split on
        commas, list of trimmed fields split on commas))); cachedFields -> .withCachedFields(java.util.Set.of("PROD_PERM"));
        maxMounts -> .withMaxMounts(1); timeout -> .withTimeout(60000) (upstream requires at least 60000 ms).
        NEVER call .withAuthServer(...): upstream TrepWsIO.withAuthServer() overwrites the username (bug); keep the connector's
        default auth server. Build lists and sets with java.util.List.of / java.util.Set.of, not Guava.
    width: 190
    height: 64
  - id: "step-pardo-2"
    type: pipeline
    position:
      x: 380
      y: 150
    data:
      label: "Compute Mid Price"
      type: STEP
      iconName: Code
      beam_transform: ParDo
      properties:
        bidField: "BID"
        askField: "ASK"
        outputField: "MID"
      system_instructions: >-
        Implement a static nested DoFn<MarketPriceMessage, MarketPriceMessage> named ComputeMidFn. For each message whose
        getFields() map contains parseable bidField and askField values, emit a new MarketPriceMessage(getId(), "Update",
        getUpdateType(), getSeqNumber(), getName(), getService(), fields map containing only outputField = (bid + ask) / 2 as a
        String, getJsonString(), getTimestamp()). Drop messages missing either field and count them with a Beam Counter
        (Metrics.counter). In the unit test use TestPipeline, Create.of(...) with MarketPriceMessage instances (constructor
        arguments: long id, String type, String updateType, long seqNumber, String name, String service, Map<String,String>
        fields, String jsonString, org.joda.time.Instant timestamp) and .withCoder(SerializableCoder.of(MarketPriceMessage.class)),
        and PAssert the MID values.
    width: 190
    height: 64
  - id: "sink-trepws-3"
    type: pipeline
    position:
      x: 680
      y: 150
    data:
      label: "Post Mid to ADS Contribution"
      type: SINK
      iconName: Radio
      beam_transform: TrepWsIO
      properties:
        hostname: "ads-contrib.acme.internal"
        port: 15000
        username: "beam-poster"
        appId: "256"
        serviceName: "DDS_TRCE"
        postMode: "offStream"
        ricMode: "fromElement"
        ricField: "name"
        fieldNames: "MID"
        ackRequired: true
        nakHandling: "log"
      system_instructions: >-
        Upstream TrepWsIO is read-only, so implement this sink as a custom static nested DoFn<MarketPriceMessage, Void> named
        TrepWebSocketPostFn over the documented Refinitiv WebSocket API, using only the JDK java.net.http WebSocket client
        (HttpClient.newHttpClient().newWebSocketBuilder().subprotocols("tr_json2")) and Jackson for JSON; add no other
        WebSocket library. Keep the WebSocket in a transient field; open it in @Setup to ws://hostname:port/WebSocket and send
        the Login request {"ID":1,"Domain":"Login","Key":{"Name":username,"Elements":{"ApplicationId":appId,"Position":<local
        host IP>}}}; close it in @Teardown. Reply to every {"Type":"Ping"} with {"Type":"Pong"}. postMode offStream means each
        element is posted on the Login stream: {"ID":1,"Type":"Post","Ack":true,"PostID":<incrementing>,"Key":{"Service":
        serviceName,"Name":<RIC>},"Message":{"ID":0,"Type":"Update","Domain":"MarketPrice","Fields":{...}}}. ricMode fromElement
        with ricField "name" means the RIC is MarketPriceMessage.getName(); fieldNames "MID" means only the MID field is posted.
        ackRequired true means track each PostID until its Ack; nakHandling "log" means log an Ack carrying a NakCode with
        LOG.warn and continue. This ADS login uses a DACS user name only, so no credential is required for this node.
    width: 190
    height: 64
edges:
  - id: "e-trep-source-to-mid"
    source: "source-trepws-1"
    target: "step-pardo-2"
  - id: "e-mid-to-trep-sink"
    source: "step-pardo-2"
    target: "sink-trepws-3"
runtimeVariables:
  - key: JOB_ID
    value: "trep-mid-price-contribution"
jobConfig:
  runner: "DirectRunner"
  machineType: "n1-standard-2"
  minInstances: 1
  maxInstances: 2
  gcsStagingPath: "gs://acme-dataflow-temp/staging"
  network: ""
  subnetwork: ""
pipelineConfig:
  language: "Java"
  outputFolder: "test/trepwsio"
  needsRebuild: false
